2026-10-10T03:57:54Z  NOTE      fix: RatingManager::save() is now called from a QGuiApplication::aboutToQuit connection added in Application::init, beside the existing aboutToQuit re-emit. The board letter said "call it from Application::quit()", but quit() is NOT the universal exit path: it only runs from the SIGINT/SIGTERM handlers invokeMethod — a QML window close or Qt.quit() ends the event loop without ever invoking that slot. aboutToQuit fires after EVERY loop exit, including quit()-driven ones (quit() ends with qapp_->quit(), verified in its tail), so one connection covers all exits. The intent — ratings survive every session end — was served; the letter adjusted, and this note records why.
2026-10-10T03:57:54Z  NOTE      load() stays at init (unchanged); the save writes the in-memory map to configDir()/ratings.toml via plain ofstream — non-atomicity and the name-keyed singleton are T0059/T0058 own items, untouched here.
2026-10-10T03:57:54Z  NOTE      tests: no machine test possible without a path-injection seam — RatingManager hardcodes file::configDir(), tests must not touch the real config dir, and the injectable redesign is T0058 prescribed scope. Verification is structural (compiles, green suite) plus the human-observable: rate a preset, quit, relaunch, the star persists.
